,friendly:[`[happy] You've a steady hand with that farm. Odette would be pleased, I think.`,`[happy] A game of chess at the inn some evening? Odo refuses to play me. He has his reasons.`,`Forty families, there were, when I was young. I mean to see the lanterns lit for that many again.`],close:[`[sad] There are things I should have said a long time ago. Not today. But soon, I hope.`,`[happy] Pip talks about you constantly. Thank you for being patient with him. His parents... well.`,`[shy] I find I sleep better since you came. That is a strange thing for an old man to admit.`],gift:{loved:`[laugh] Oh my. A {gift}! You have been asking about me. Thank you, truly.`,liked:`[happy] How very kind. I shall enjoy this.`,neutral:`Thank you. That is thoughtful of you.`,disliked:`[sad] Ah. I'd... rather not keep this, if it's all the same. But thank you.`}},pip:{intro:`[laugh] Ahoy! Are you the new farmer? I'm Pip. I'm going to be a pirate. Have you seen the white bird? It's MINE. I saw it first.`,stranger:[`[angry] Grandpa says I can't go past the mist. That's exactly what a pirate WOULDN'T listen to.`,`[happy] Do you have any frogs? I'm collecting them. Grandpa says not in the house.`,`[happy] Kit draws the maps and I find the treasure. That is the deal.`],friendly:[`[surprised] The white bird looked at me today. Like, LOOKED at me. Birds don't do that.`,`[laugh] You can be in my crew. You have to swear an oath. It's fine, it's a short one.`,`[sad] My mum and dad are coming back after summer. They said. It's been a lot of summers.`],close:[`[surprised] I followed the heron to the old shrine and it glowed. Not the bird. The SHRINE. Promise you believe me.`,`[laugh] You're my first mate now. That's the most important job on a ship.`,`[sad] Sometimes I pretend the boat that comes on Tideday is my parents. It's never them. But it's okay because you're here.`],gift:{loved:`[laugh] WHOA. A {gift}! This is going in the treasure chest. The REAL one.`,liked:`[happy] Cool! Thanks!`,neutral:`[sad] Oh. Um. Thanks, I guess. It's not treasure though.`,disliked:`[angry] Eww! Why would you give me this?`}},maren:{intro:`You're Odette's boy, then. Maren Ashby, the forge. If your tools break, bring them here. If you want small talk, try the inn.`,stranger:[`[angry] Busy. Unless you need something smithed, make it quick.`,`Iron does what you tell it, if you know how to tell it. People are harder.`,`[angry] Don't stand there. Sparks.`],friendly:[`[laugh] Ha. You're stubborn. I like that more than I'd like to admit.`,`[happy] There was a storm out at sea last night. Best sound in the world, thunder over the forge.`,`My dad was the best miner on this island before Hollowdeep took his leg. Don't let him tell you otherwise. Actually, he'll tell you exactly that.`],close:[`[shy] ...Fine. Look. I make these. Little rings. Nobody's seen them. Don't laugh.`,`[sad] Clara Corran keeps trying to say hello. I don't know what I'm supposed to do with that.`,`[shy] You're the only one who doesn't talk to me like I'm about to swing a hammer. I might, though. Kidding.`],gift:{loved:`[laugh] Now THIS is a gift. A {gift}. You actually pay attention, huh?`,liked:`[happy] Not bad. I'll take it.`,neutral:`Huh. Okay. Thanks.`,disliked:`[angry] What am I supposed to do with this? Don't flatter me, just bring me something useful.`}},odo:{intro:`Hmph. Another Odette, are you? Same eyes. Odo Ashby. I carve wood now. Used to cut stone, before the mine decided it wanted my leg.`,stranger:[`[sad] Back in my day the crystals sang down there. Nobody believes me. Suit yourself.`,`Mind the step. I always mind the step now.`,`[angry] Don't trust the man in the fancy coat. I've seen that look before, on his kind.`],friendly:[`[happy] Pull up a crate. I'll tell you about the night the third shaft lit up blue.`,`[happy] You fish? A bit of fried fish and a pipe on the porch. That's living.`,`[angry] Bram Hollis knows more than he says. Always has. Always will.`],close:[`I've a map of Hollowdeep. Every tunnel. Never shown a soul. Maybe one day you'll need it.`,`[happy] Maren thinks I don't see her making those little rings at night. I see. I'm proud of her. Don't tell her.`,`[sad] Your grandmother came to me before she vanished. Asked about the lower shafts. I wish I'd asked her why.`],gift:{loved:`[happy] Well now. A {gift}. You've been talking to someone who knows me. ...Thank you.`,liked:`Hm. That'll do nicely.`,neutral:`Hm. Thanks.`,disliked:`[angry] Bah! Take it to Bram, he'll like that sort of thing.`}},clara:{intro:`Hello. Clara Corran. I run the workshop in the old boatshed. If you need anything built, I'll build it right. Not fast. Right.`,stranger:[`Good timber on this island. That is why I came back. Mostly.`,`Measure twice, cut once. My father's rule. Still the best one.`,`[sad] People are polite to me here. Polite isn't the same as friendly.`],friendly:[`[happy] There is something about mornings in the workshop. Sawdust in the light. Quiet.`,`Do you like maps? I've been collecting old ones of the island. The mist walls keep moving.`,`[sad] Maren Ashby hates me. I understand why. I wish she knew what I know.`],close:[`[sad] I did not come back for the timber. I came back for my father. I think you guessed that.`,`[shy] This ruler was his. I measure everything with it. Silly, maybe.`,`[shy] I don't say it often, but I'm glad you're here. Things feel less like they're falling apart.`],gift:{loved:`[shy] A {gift}... You remembered. That means more than you know.`,liked:`[happy] Thank you. That is a good choice.`,neutral:`Thanks. I can find a use for it.`,disliked:`[sad] I'd rather you hadn't. But thank you for the thought.`}},lia:{intro:`[laugh] Hey there, farmer! Lia Tamsin. I fish the cove. If you hear singing at the dock, that's me, and yes, I know I'm off-key.`,stranger:[`[angry] Fish are biting near the rocks today. Or they were, before Silas Crane brought his big noisy boat in.`,`[surprised] Oh, is it morning? I lose track. The tide keeps better time than I do.`,`[laugh] Yo ho, and a bottle of... tea. Mum says no rum before noon.`],friendly:[`[sad] Everyone I grew up with left. You're the first new face in years. It's nice.`,`[happy] Want to see the sunset from the end of the dock some time? Best seat on the island.`,`[surprised] I've seen lights under the water in the cove. At night. Don't look at me like that.`],close:[`[shy] I write poems. Bad ones. Okay, I'll read you one. Just one. Don't you dare laugh.`,`[shy] Sometimes I think I stayed for Mum. Lately I think I stayed for something else. Maybe someone.`,`[surprised] The lights in the cove are getting brighter. Come with me tonight and see?`],gift:{loved:`[laugh] No way, a {gift}! You've got good taste. Come here, you!`,liked:`[happy] Aw, thanks! That made my day.`,neutral:`[happy] Ha, okay! Thanks, I guess!`,disliked:`[sad] Ugh, that's... not really my thing. You're sweet for trying though.`}},nell:{intro:`[laugh] Oh, look at you! You've Odette's chin, you have. I'm Nell, I run the Lantern & Tide. Come by for supper, and don't you dare say you can't afford it.`,stranger:[`[surprised] Have you eaten? You look like you haven't eaten. Nobody eats properly on a farm.`,`[laugh] Rooms upstairs, chowder downstairs, gossip everywhere. That is an inn.`,`Lia's off at the dock again, I expect. That girl and the sea.`],friendly:[`[sad] Your grandmother sat in that corner every Sunday. Chowder, extra herbs. Every Sunday.`,`[happy] I remember every birthday on this island. Yours too, now. Don't think I won't bake.`,`[sad] We used to dance every festival. Haven't had enough people for a proper reel in years.`],close:[`[sad] Odette came by the night she disappeared. She was frightened. I've never told anyone that.`,`[happy] Lia's been smiling more since you came. A mother notices. That's all I'll say.`,`[sad] I lost my husband to a storm. Some days the inn is the only thing that keeps my hands busy. You help, love.`],gift:{loved:`[laugh] Oh, a {gift}! Love, you shouldn't have. No, really, I'm going to cry. Come here.`,liked:`[happy] Well, aren't you sweet! Thank you, dear.`,neutral:`Thank you, love. That's kind.`,disliked:`[angry] Oh. Well. Waste not, I suppose. Don't do it again.`}},hazel:{intro:`[laugh] HEY! You're the new farmer! Hazel Penrose, Penrose Ranch. Healthiest cows on the coast. Don't let anyone tell you this island's dying, 'cause it's not!`,stranger:[`[happy] I've been up since four. Animals don't sleep in and neither do I.`,`[laugh] Clover had a calf last week. Strong little thing. I named her Thunder.`,`[angry] I'm bringing back the Spring Fair. Nobody believes me. Watch me.`],friendly:[`[laugh] Race you to the well! ...Okay, I'll give you a head start. A small one.`,`[happy] You've got good hands for animals, I can tell. Come by the ranch sometime.`,`[surprised] Gran's been humming old songs again. Strange ones. She won't tell me where she learned them.`],close:[`[sad] Some nights I wonder if I'm wrong. If it is dying. Then I see you out there working and I think, nope.`,`[shy] You're not a quitter. I like that. I like you. ...Ugh, forget I said that. Go feed your animals.`,`[laugh] When the Fair comes back, you're my partner for the three-legged race. Non-negotiable.`],gift:{loved:`[laugh] A {gift}?! Yes! This is the best thing anyone has ever given me! Probably!`,liked:`[happy] Hey, thanks! You're alright.`,neutral:`Oh! Thanks. I'll find somewhere to put that.`,disliked:`[angry] Bleh. No offence, but no thanks.`}},edda:{intro:`[angry] Eh? Speak up. Odette's grandson, are you? Hmph. Edda Penrose. I weave. Mind your boots on my floor.`,stranger:[`Back when there were forty families, every one of them had a Penrose blanket.`,`[angry] What? No, I didn't hear you. Try again with better manners.`,`[surprised] These patterns? I just like the shapes. Don't read into it.`],friendly:[`[sad] Your grandmother grew lavender by the farmhouse. Finest on the island. I miss the smell of it.`,`Hazel works too hard. Like her mother. Don't tell her I said so.`,`[sad] There was a song my mother sang. About a heron and a lady in the mist. I can't remember the end.`],close:[`[happy] Sit, child. My hands are slow now, but they remember things my head forgets.`,`The patterns aren't just shapes. You knew that. Odette knew it too.`,`[surprised] The end of the song goes... no. Not yet. When you've seen the shrines, come back to me.`],gift:{loved:`[surprised] Oh! A {gift}. Well. Well, well. Sit down, I'll put the kettle on.`,liked:`[happy] Hmph. Good. That will do nicely.`,neutral:`Mm. Thank you.`,disliked:`[angry] What's this rubbish? Take it away before I trip on it.`}},fen:{intro:`[laugh] Welcome, welcome! Fen Dobbs, Dobbs General Store! Seeds, supplies, and the second-best jokes on the island. Rosa has the best ones. She says she doesn't.`,stranger:[`[laugh] Why did the scarecrow win an award? He was outstanding in his field! ...You're a farmer, that one's for you.`,`[happy] Seeds, tools, bargains! Well. Mostly seeds.`,`[surprised] Shipping box is by the door. Silas Crane pays well. Very well. Almost too well.`],friendly:[`[sad] Business has been slow. But you've brought a bit of life back, I'll say that.`,`Seven down: a dish best served at the inn. Five letters. Any ideas?`,`[shy] I run a tab for half the village. Can't help it. Rosa says I'm a soft touch.`],close:[`[sad] Silas made me an offer for the shop. A good one. I haven't told Rosa. I don't know what to do.`,`[happy] You're good for this place. Don't let anyone tell you otherwise. Not even me on a bad day.`,`[laugh] Rosa and I met at the Lantern Festival thirty years ago. Biggest bargain I ever got.`],gift:{loved:`[laugh] A {gift}! For me? Now that's what I call a bargain!`,liked:`[happy] Oh, thank you! I could get used to this.`,neutral:`[happy] Ha, thank you kindly!`,disliked:`[sad] Er. I'll... put it on the clearance shelf.`}},rosa:{intro:`Good day. Rosa Dobbs. I sew. If Fen has sold you something you did not need, bring it back to me and I will sort it out.`,stranger:[`[angry] Please don't track mud in. I've just finished a hem.`,`A good seam is invisible. A bad one is all anyone sees.`,`[happy] Fen is telling jokes again. I can hear it from here.`],friendly:[`[sad] I made every festival costume in this village for twenty years. I miss the work.`,`[happy] Quiet afternoons. Lavender tea. A good bolt of cloth. That's all I need.`,`Fen worries about the shop more than he lets on. Thank you for coming in.`],close:[`[surprised] Your grandmother asked me to sew a hidden pocket into her coat once. I never asked why.`,`[happy] I would like to make you something. Let me take your measurements. Hold still.`,`Fen has been keeping a secret from me. He thinks I don't know. I always know.`],gift:{loved:`[happy] A {gift}. Oh, that is lovely. Thank you, really.`,liked:`[happy] How thoughtful. Thank you.`,neutral:`Thank you.`,disliked:`[angry] Oh dear. Please, not near the fabric.`}},ilse:{intro:`Dr. Ilse Varga. The clinic is across the plaza. If you're about to tell me the mist is a goddess, save it. I've heard it.`,stranger:[`[angry] Get some sleep. Farmers never do. Then they end up in my waiting room.`,`Coffee. Black. Any other questions?`,`[happy] The mist is fog with good publicity. Probably.`],friendly:[`[sad] I came from the mainland. I'd prefer not to discuss why. I'm told that makes me mysterious.`,`Kit has been mapping the mist walls. His maps say they move. Fog moves. That is all it is.`,`[happy] You look healthier than most people on this island. Keep it up. Fewer patients for me.`],close:[`[surprised] I took a reading near the shrine last week. The numbers made no sense. I've been checking my instruments ever since.`,`[shy] Kit adores you. He doesn't adore people. Thank you.`,`[angry] If you tell anyone I said the shrine might be... something, I'll deny it. Medically.`],gift:{loved:`[happy] A {gift}. Hm. You have good instincts. Thank you.`,liked:`Thank you. That is genuinely useful.`,neutral:`Thanks.`,disliked:`[angry] Please don't bring superstitious nonsense into my clinic. Or this. Whatever this is.`}},kit:{intro:`...Hi. I'm Kit. I make maps. The mist walls move, you know. Nobody believes me except Pip, and Pip believes everything.`,stranger:[`[surprised] Shh. There's a beetle. ...Okay, it's gone.`,`[angry] I'm not too young to go past the mist. I'm ten.`,`[happy] Pip is loud. I like him anyway.`],friendly:[`[happy] Here, I drew the path to your farm. It's more accurate than Grandpa Bram's.`,`[happy] I like rainy days. The beetles come out and nobody shouts.`,`[surprised] The mist wall by the meadows moved three steps west since last week. I measured.`],close:[`[happy] I made a map with all the shrines on it. Four, plus a big one in the middle. Want to see?`,`[sad] Mum says the mist is just weather. I don't think she believes it anymore.`,`[shy] You're my favourite grown-up. Don't tell Wren. Or Pip.`],gift:{loved:`[laugh] A {gift}! ...Can I keep it forever?`,liked:`Oh. Thanks. That's nice.`,neutral:`Okay. Thank you.`,disliked:`[sad] I don't like that. Sorry.`}},wren:{intro:`[surprised] Oh! Sorry, I was reading. Wren Calloway. I teach at the schoolhouse and look after the archive. You're Odette's grandson? She used to borrow my books. She always brought them back.`,stranger:[`[laugh] These glyphs are the oldest writing on the island. I've translated eleven words in three years. It's going well!`,`Morning lessons, archive in the afternoon, tea in between. Lots of tea.`,`[sad] Please don't shout near the schoolhouse. Pip does enough of that.`],friendly:[`[laugh] This glyph means "veil". Or "mist". Or possibly "laundry". Context matters.`,`I came to the island to study for one summer. That was three summers ago.`,`[happy] Do you like lighthouses? There was one on the north cliff. I'd love to see it someday.`],close:[`[surprised] I found Odette's handwriting in the margins of the shrine records. She was translating them too.`,`[shy] You make it easier to be brave. I'm not usually brave. I'm usually in the archive.`,`[shy] When this is all over, will you climb to the old lighthouse with me? It's a date. I mean, a plan. A date-plan.`],gift:{loved:`[laugh] A {gift}! Oh, this is wonderful. I'm going to catalogue it. And then keep it forever.`,liked:`[happy] Oh, thank you! How lovely.`,neutral:`Thank you. That's very kind.`,disliked:`[sad] Oh. Oh no. Thank you, but... no.`}},ivy:{intro:`[laugh] Hey! You came in on the same boat as me! Ivy Brightwater, engineer. I'm fixing the old waterwheel. Don't touch anything. Seriously.`,stranger:[`[laugh] Did you hear that bang? Totally on purpose. Controlled. Mostly.`,`[happy] Manuals are for people who don't take things apart.`,`[surprised] Lamps that never go out. That's what I heard. That's why I'm here.`],friendly:[`[laugh] Strong tea, a box of gears and a waterwheel. Best day in a month.`,`[surprised] You've got good hands. Want to hold this? Don't let go. Don't. Let. Go.`,`Mainland engineers would kill for the crystals on this island. Which is exactly why I don't tell them.`],close:[`[happy] I'm designing something big. Light-big. I'll need your help. And copper. Mostly copper.`,`[shy] Nobody's ever been this patient with me. I'm loud and I break things. You don't seem to mind.`,`[happy] When the wheel turns, you're the first one I'm showing. That's a promise.`],gift:{loved:`[laugh] A {gift}?! You absolute legend! I'm building something with this. Immediately.`,liked:`[happy] Ooh, useful! Thanks!`,neutral:`Huh. Cool. Thanks!`,disliked:`[angry] Ugh, what? No. Hard pass.`}},amara:{intro:`[happy] Peace be with you. I am Sister Amara, keeper of Mirael's chapel. Your grandmother walked the shrines more than any of us. I hope you will be... gentler with them.`,stranger:[`[sad] The goddess has been silent forty years. I still light the candles.`,`Slowly, child. Nothing here was ever rushed and made better for it.`,`[sad] The white heron comes to the chapel steps some mornings. I do not know what that means anymore.`],friendly:[`[sad] Odette asked me things about the shrines the chapel never approved of. I said no. I'm not sure I was right.`,`[happy] Silence is a kind of prayer. So is work. You pray well with that farm.`,`There are four shrines and the Heart. Most people here have forgotten even that.`],close:[`[surprised] Last night the Root Shrine felt warm. I have not felt that since I was a girl.`,`[happy] Forty years is a long time to keep faith. You've made the last few easier.`,`If Mirael speaks again, I think she will speak to you first.`],gift:{loved:`[happy] A {gift}. Bless you, child. This will sit by the altar.`,liked:`[happy] Thank you. That is a kind gift.`,neutral:`Thank you.`,disliked:`[sad] I would rather not. But I thank you for the thought.`}},silas:{intro:`[happy] Well, well. A new face. Silas Crane, Grayhaven Trading Company, at your service. Anything you grow, I'll buy. Anything you find in the hills, I'll buy for more.`,stranger:[`[angry] Mud. Everywhere, mud. How do you people live like this?`,`[happy] I pay a fair price. Better than fair. Ask anyone. Well. Ask Fen.`,`[angry] That old man by the forge stares at me as if I owe him something.`],friendly:[`[happy] Find any crystals in your travels? Glowing ones? I'd make it very worth your while.`,`[happy] You're sharper than the rest of them. I appreciate that in a business partner.`,`My great-great-great-grandfather started the company with one crystal. Family legend. Probably nonsense.`],close:[`[sad] The board wants results. The company's crystal is dimming. I don't know why I'm telling you this.`,`[sad] Sometimes I wonder what my family really took from this island.`,`[sad] You're the only one here who doesn't look at me like a thief. I hope I don't prove you wrong.`],gift:{loved:`[laugh] A {gift}! Now THIS is quality. You and I will get along famously.`,liked:`[happy] How generous. I shall remember this.`,neutral:`Ah. Thank you. How... rustic.`,disliked:`[angry] 