:2.6,lookHeight:1.5}},{fade:`in`},{say:`narrator`,text:`Half of Willowmere came in its Sunday best. The other half came straight from work, and nobody minded.`},{camera:{from:[25.2,-16.5],look:[28,-19.6],height:1.8,lookHeight:1.5}},{say:`amara`,text:`[happy] Friends. Mirael has watched over this island for a thousand years, and she likes nothing better than two people choosing each other.`},{say:`amara`,text:`${n}. Will you take this farmer, his muddy boots and his stubborn field, for all the seasons to come?`},...e.vows,{say:`amara`,text:`[happy] And you? Will you take her, for all the seasons to come?`},{choice:[{label:`I will.`},{label:`With all my heart.`,then:[{say:t,text:`[shy] ...Show-off.`}]}]},{actor:`heron`,at:[46,-32],height:12,face:Ez},{say:`amara`,text:`[surprised] Oh, look. Look who came.`},{camera:{from:[24.6,-15.4],look:Az,height:1.7,lookHeight:1.2}},{walk:`heron`,to:Az,speed:7,height:0},{face:`heron`,to:Oz},{wait:.8},{say:`amara`,text:`[laugh] Well. I think that settles it. By the grace of Mirael and her heron: you are married!`},{camera:{from:[26,-16.2],look:[28,-18.8],height:1.7,lookHeight:1.6}},...e.afterVows,{say:`narrator`,text:`Pip threw a whole basket of petals at once. Most of them landed on Bram.`},{fade:`out`},{exit:`heron`},{exit:`amara`},...r.map(e=>({exit:e})),{exit:t},{camera:`player`},{title:`${n} moves to Thistledown`,subtitle:`She will be home whenever she is not at work`},{fade:`in`}],outcome:[{flag:Pz.married(e.id)},{unflag:Pz.engaged(e.id)}]}}function Rz(e,t){let{id:n}=e,r=Mz(n),i=t===1?Nz.wedding(n):Nz.birth(n,1);return[{id:Nz.baby(n,t),kind:`romance`,story:`Family`,title:t===1?`A Bigger Family`:`Another Little One`,requires:[{done:i},{daysSince:{event:i,min:t===1?7:28}}],trigger:{ask:n,label:t===1?`Talk about having a baby`:`Talk about another baby`},lead:t===1?`Thistledown has room for more. Talk with ${r} about a baby, when you're both ready.`:`There's room for one more at Thistledown, if you and ${r} want.`,summary:t===1?`You and ${r} decided to start a family.`:`You and ${r} decided on one more.`,cutscene:e.baby[t-1]},{id:Nz.birth(n,t),kind:`romance`,story:`Family`,title:t===1?`Welcome Home`:`Welcome Home, Again`,requires:{done:Nz.baby(n,t)},when:[{daysSince:{event:Nz.baby(n,t),min:14}},{hour:[6,22]}],trigger:`auto`,lead:`The baby is due 14 days after you talked. Ilse at the clinic says ${r} is doing beautifully.`,summary:`Your ${`{kin`+t+`}`}, {child${t}}, was born at Thistledown.`,hints:[{from:`ilse`,text:`[happy] ${r} is doing splendidly. Any day now. Keep your boots by the door.`}],cutscene:[{fade:`out`},{say:`narrator`,text:`Ilse came running up the road from the clinic to find you. "It's time," was all she said, and you ran.`},{title:`Thistledown`,subtitle:t===1?`A new voice in the farmhouse`:`Another new voice in the farmhouse`},{do:{birth:!0}},{say:`narrator`,text:`The baby was born just as the kettle boiled: tiny, furious, and perfect. A {kin}.`},...e.newborn,{say:n,text:`[happy] Go on, then. What shall we call them?`},{nameChild:!0},{say:n,text:`[happy] {child}. Hello, {child}. Welcome to Thistledown.`},{fade:`in`}]}]}var zz={maren:{id:`maren`,hearts:[{title:`The Bellows`,summary:`Maren let you work the forge bellows. She took over the forge at sixteen, when her dad could no longer work.`,hints:[{from:`odo`,text:`[laugh] My girl's been swearing at a weld all morning. Go and say hello. She'll pretend to hate it.`}],cutscene:[{say:`maren`,text:`[angry] Blast it. Cold weld. Again.`},{say:`maren`,text:`You. Don't just stand there. Grab the bellows handle and pump when I say. Not before. Not after.`},{choice:[{label:`Pump the bellows.`,then:[{say:`narrator`,text:`The coals roared white. Maren struck, turned, struck again, and the seam closed like it had never been broken.`},{say:`maren`,text:`[laugh] Ha! Not bad. Your rhythm's terrible, but you listen. That's rarer.`},{do:{friendship:`maren`,points:40}}]},{label:`Is this safe?`,then:[{say:`maren`,text:`[angry] No. Pump.`},{say:`narrator`,text:`You pumped. The seam closed. Maren looked very slightly impressed, and then annoyed at herself for it.`}]}]},{say:`maren`,text:`I was sixteen the first time I did that on my own. Dad couldn't stand at the anvil any more, so somebody had to.`},{say:`maren`,text:`[shy] ...Don't make a face. I'm not after sympathy. Come back and pump again some time. You were useful.`}]},{title:`The Little Ring`,summary:`You caught Maren making a tiny silver ring with tweezers. Nobody else has ever seen her jewellery.`,cutscene:[{say:`narrator`,text:`Maren was hunched over the bench, not at the anvil, holding something very small in a pair of tweezers.`},{say:`maren`,text:`[surprised] What? No. Nothing. Go away.`},{say:`narrator`,text:`It was a ring no wider than a fingernail: a silver band twisted like a wave, with a speck of blue glass set in it.`},{choice:[{label:`It's beautiful.`,then:[{say:`maren`,text:`[shy] ...It is not. The setting's crooked. See? There.`},{say:`maren`,text:`[shy] Fine. It's a little bit beautiful. Shut up.`},{do:{friendship:`maren`,points:50}}]},{label:`Who is it for?`,then:[{say:`maren`,text:`Nobody. Me. ...Nobody. I make them and I put them in a box. That's the whole story.`},{do:{friendship:`maren`,points:20}}]}]},{say:`maren`,text:`Big hands, small work. People laugh. So I don't show people.`},{say:`maren`,text:`[angry] You didn't see this. If Pip finds out, the whole island knows by supper.`}]},{title:`Thunder`,summary:`Maren watched a storm roll in with you and told you about the day Hollowdeep took her father's leg.`,hints:[{from:`odo`,text:`[sad] She doesn't talk about the mine. Not to me, anyway. Maybe she would to you.`}],cutscene:[{say:`maren`,text:`[happy] Smell that? Storm coming in off the sea. Stand here, by the door. Best seat on the island.`},{say:`narrator`,text:`Thunder rolled over the forge roof. Maren closed her eyes and grinned like it was music.`},{say:`maren`,text:`[sad] It was a day like this when the cave-in happened. I was fourteen. They carried Dad up out of Hollowdeep on a door.`},{say:`maren`,text:`[angry] Everyone said the Corrans cut corners on the props. Tomas Corran left the island a month later. Says it all, doesn't it?`},{choice:[{label:`That's a lot to carry on your own.`,then:[{say:`maren`,text:`[sad] ...Yeah. It is. Nobody's ever said that. They say 'poor Odo' and look at me like I'll break something.`},{do:{friendship:`maren`,points:50}}]},{label:`Clara seems decent, though.`,then:[{say:`maren`,text:`[angry] Don't. Not today.`},{say:`maren`,text:`[sad] ...Maybe. I don't know. That's the worst part. I don't know.`}]}]},{say:`maren`,text:`[shy] Stay till it passes? I don't mind the company. Yours, I mean. Not everyone's.`}]},{title:`Ashby Fire Stew`,summary:`Maren made you her fiery stew and admitted, in her own way, that she likes having you around.`,cutscene:[{say:`maren`,text:`You eat spicy food? Don't answer. You're about to find out.`},{say:`narrator`,text:`She ladled out something dark red from a pot on the forge coals. The steam alone made your eyes water.`},{choice:[{label:`Eat it all.`,then:[{say:`narrator`,text:`It was the hottest thing you have ever eaten. It was also very, very good. You finished the bowl.`},{say:`maren`,text:`[laugh] HA! You actually finished it! Dad cried the first time. Don't tell him I told you.`},{do:{friendship:`maren`,points:60}}]},{label:`Ask for water.`,then:[{say:`maren`,text:`[laugh] Water makes it worse. Here. Bread. Lightweight.`},{do:{friendship:`maren`,points:30}}]}]},{say:`maren`,text:`[shy] Look. I'm not good at this. I like it when you come by. The forge is quieter when you're not here, and I don't like the quiet any more.`},{say:`maren`,text:`[angry] That's all. Don't make it weird. Go on. Shoo.`}]},{title:`Made by Hand`,summary:`Maren gave you a ring she made for you. Every other ring she ever made was for nobody.`,lead:`You're courting Maren. Keep seeing her (10 hearts).`,cutscene:[{say:`maren`,text:`[shy] Hold out your hand. No, the other one. Stop smiling.`},{say:`narrator`,text:`She pressed something warm into your palm: a plain iron ring, hammered smooth, with a thin line of silver running all the way round.`},{say:`maren`,text:`Iron, because it's honest. Silver, because... because I wanted it to be pretty. For once.`},{say:`maren`,text:`[sad] I've got a whole box of rings I made for nobody. This one I made for you.`},{choice:[{label:`I'll never take it off.`,then:[{say:`maren`,text:`[shy] You will when you farm. Rust. ...But thanks.`}]},{label:`Kiss her on the cheek.`,then:[{say:`maren`,text:`[surprised] ...! You... soot. You've got soot on your nose now. Idiot. Come here.`}]}]},{do:{flag:`key:ring-maren`}}]}],bouquet:[{say:`maren`,text:`[surprised] Flowers? For me? I tell everyone I hate flowers.`},{say:`maren`,text:`[shy] ...I tell everyone else that.`},{say:`narrator`,text:`She held the bouquet like it might break, very carefully, at arm's length.`},{say:`maren`,text:`[happy] Yes. Fine. Yes. We're... whatever this is. Courting. Don't tell Dad. He'll tell everyone.`}],proposal:[{say:`maren`,text:`[surprised] That's a heron pendant. You know what that means here, right? You can't just... that means forever.`},{say:`maren`,text:`[sad] I'm loud and I'm stubborn and I smell like coal. I won't change for anyone.`},{say:`player`,text:`I don't want you to change. I want you.`},{say:`maren`,text:`[shy] ...You absolute idiot. Yes. YES. Don't cry. I'm not crying. It's the forge.`}],vows:[{say:`maren`,text:`[shy] I'm not good with words. I'm good with iron. So here it is: I'll keep your tools sharp, and I'll never once pretend with you.`},{say:`maren`,text:`I will.`}],afterVows:[{say:`maren`,text:`[laugh] Dad's crying. Don't look at him. He'll deny it till the day he dies.`},{say:`maren`,text:`[shy] ...Husband. Huh. I could get used to that.`}],family:[`odo`],baby:[[{say:`maren`,text:`[surprised] A baby? You and me? I can barely keep a fern alive.`},{say:`maren`,text:`[happy] ...Dad would carve them a whole wooden zoo. He'd be unbearable.`},{say:`maren`,text:`[shy] Yeah. Let's. Let's do it.`}],[{say:`maren`,text:`[laugh] Another one? {child} already runs this house.`},{say:`maren`,text:`[shy] ...Fine. Two little blacksmiths. The forge could use the help.`}]],newborn:[{say:`maren`,text:`[laugh] Look at those fists. Born to work a forge. That's an Ashby grip.`}],courting:[`[shy] You came by. Good. I mean, fine. Good.`,`[laugh] Dad keeps asking when you're coming to supper. I keep telling him never. He knows I'm lying.`,`[happy] Brought you a sharpened hoe. Don't make a fuss. It was dull and it bothered me.`],married:[`[happy] Morning. Coffee's on the stove. I burnt the toast, so don't eat that.`,`[laugh] I keep reaching for the anvil in our kitchen. It's a table. I know it's a table.`,`[shy] I like coming home and seeing your boots by the door. That's all. That's the whole thought.`,`[happy] Storm tonight, I think. We could sit on the porch and watch it come in.`,`Dad came by. He says the farm looks better than it has in years. He also says you owe him a game of cards.`],gifts:[{item:`iron-ore`,line:`[happy] Found this on my way home. Iron ore. Don't say I never give you anything.`},{item:`copper-ore`,line:`[happy] Spare copper from the forge. Put it to use.`}]},clara:Tz,lia:{id:`lia`,hearts:[{title:`Off-Key`,summary:`Lia taught you the chorus of a sea shanty. Neither of you can sing. It didn't matter.`,cutscene:[{say:`lia`,text:`[laugh] Oh good, a crew! I need someone for the chorus. Every shanty needs a chorus. Ready?`},{say:`lia`,text:`"Oh the mist rolled in at Gullwing Cove, and the boats all lost their way..."`},{choice:[{label:`Sing the chorus, loudly.`,then:[{say:`player`,text:`"...HEAVE AWAY, me lads, HEAVE AWAY!"`},{say:`lia`,text:`[laugh] HA! You're worse than me! That's wonderful! Nobody's ever been worse than me!`},{do:{friendship:`lia`,points:50}}]},{label:`Clap along.`,then:[{say:`lia`,text:`[happy] A rhythm section! Okay, okay. I'll take it. Next time you're singing.`},{do:{friendship:`lia`,points:20}}]}]},{say:`lia`,text:`[sad] It used to be six of us singing that, out on the rocks. Then there was one. It's nice to have two again.`}]},{title:`Always Late`,summary:`Lia admitted why she's always late: she can't stop watching the sea, in case something comes back.`,hints:[{from:`nell`,text:`[angry] Lia was meant to bring the morning catch to the inn at seven. It's ten. Have you seen her? Of course you have, she's on that pier.`}],cutscene:[{say:`lia`,text:`[surprised] Is it ten already? Mum's going to kill me. I was bringing her the catch. Hours ago. In theory.`},{say:`lia`,text:`[sad] I always mean to be on time. And then I look at the water and it's suddenly afternoon.`},{say:`player`,text:`What are you looking for out there?`},{say:`lia`,text:`[sad] Boats, I suppose. Everyone I grew up with sailed off one by one. I keep thinking one of them will sail back.`},{choice:[{label:`Someone sailed in, at least.`,then:[{say:`lia`,text:`[shy] ...Yeah. Someone did. Huh. I hadn't thought of it like that.`},{do:{friendship:`lia`,points:50}}]},{label:`Let's take your mum the fish together.`,then:[{say:`lia`,text:`[laugh] She can't yell at me with you there! You're a genius!`},{do:{friendship:`lia`,points:40}}]}]}]},{title:`Sunset on the Pier`,summary:`You watched the sunset with Lia from the end of the pier. She told you why she stayed when everyone else left.`,lead:`Lia loves the sunset from the end of the pier. Find her there in the evening, after 5 pm (6 hearts).`,when:{hour:[17,22]},cutscene:[{say:`lia`,text:`[happy] You came! Sit here, legs over the edge. Best seat on the island, I promise.`},{say:`narrator`,text:`The sun slid down into the mist, and for a moment the whole sea turned the colour of peaches.`},{say:`lia`,text:`[sad] When the others left, they asked me to come. I said no. I told them it was for Mum.`},{say:`lia`,text:`It wasn't, really. I just couldn't leave the sea. It felt like it was waiting for something. Silly, huh?`},{choice:[{label:`It's not silly.`,then:[{say:`lia`,text:`[shy] ...Okay. Then I won't feel silly. Not with you.`},{do:{friendship:`lia`,points:50}}]},{label:`Maybe it was waiting for me.`,then:[{say:`lia`,text:`[laugh] Oh, listen to you! ...Maybe. Maybe it was.`},{do:{friendship:`lia`,points:50}}]}]}]},{title:`A Bad Poem`,summary:`Lia read you one of her poems. It was about you, though she wouldn't say so.`,cutscene:[{say:`lia`,text:`[shy] Okay. Okay okay okay. I said I'd read you one. Don't laugh. If you laugh I'm jumping in the sea.`},{say:`narrator`,text:`She opened the battered notebook, cleared her throat twice, and read very fast.`},{say:`lia`,text:`"The tide comes in, the tide goes out, / and I stay put, like I always do. / Then one grey day a boat came through / and the fog went quiet, and so did I."`},{say:`lia`,text:`[shy] ...That's it. That's the poem. It's bad. It's about nothing. It's about boats.`},{choice:[{label:`It's about me, isn't it?`,then:[{say:`lia`,text:`[shy] ...Maybe a little bit. Fine. A lot. Don't look at me.`},{do:{friendship:`lia`,points:60}}]},{label:`It's lovely.`,then:[{say:`lia`,text:`[happy] You think so? Really? ...I'll write you a better one. One day.`},{do:{friendship:`lia`,points:40}}]}]}]},{title:`Sea Glass`,summary:`Lia gave you a piece of green sea glass she found on the morning your boat came in.`,lead:`You're courting Lia. Keep seeing her (10 hearts).`,cutscene:[{say:`lia`,text:`[shy] Hold out your hand. Close your eyes. No peeking.`},{say:`narrator`,text:`Something cool and smooth: a piece of sea glass, green as her eyes, worn soft by the tide.`},{say:`lia`,text:`I found that on the beach the morning your boat came in through the mist. I've carried it ever since. I didn't know why.`},{say:`lia`,text:`[happy] I know why now. Keep it. It's yours. It always was, I think.`},{choice:[{label:`I'll keep it forever.`},{label:`Kiss her.`,then:[{say:`lia`,text:`[laugh] ...Wow. Okay. I forgot what I was saying. Something about glass?`}]}]},{do:{flag:`key:glass-lia`}}]}],bouquet:[{say:`lia`,text:`[surprised] Are those for me? Flowers? For actual me?`},{say:`lia`,text:`[laugh] Nobody's given me flowers since... ever, I think. Ever.`},{say:`lia`,text:`[shy] Yes. Yes yes yes. I'll even try to be on time. For you. Sometimes.`}],proposal:[{say:`lia`,text:`[surprised] A heron pendant? Oh. Oh no. I'm going to cry. I'm crying. Look what you did.`},{say:`lia`,text:`[happy] Of course I will. I've been waiting on this pier for something my whole life. It was you, you idiot.`}],vows:[{say:`lia`,text:`[shy] I always stay. That's my thing. Everyone leaves, and I stay.`},{say:`lia`,text:`[happy] So I'll stay with you. Every tide, every season. I will. And I'll even be on time for it.`}],afterVows:[{say:`lia`,text:`[laugh] Mum's already planning the fish pie. For the whole village. She's been planning it for years, I think.`},{say:`lia`,text:`[shy] Husband. Huh. That one's going in a poem.`}],family:[`nell`],baby:[[{say:`lia`,text:`[surprised] A baby? A little one, on the farm, with your eyes and my terrible singing?`},{say:`lia`,text:`[happy] Yes. Oh, yes. I'll teach them every shanty. Even the rude ones. Especially the rude ones.`}],[{say:`lia`,text:`[laugh] Another one? {child} needs someone to sing the chorus with.`},{say:`lia`,text:`[happy] Let's. A whole crew.`}]],newborn:[{say:`lia`,text:`[happy] Listen to those lungs. That's a sea voice. That's a shanty voice.`}],courting:[`[happy] I was only twenty minutes late today! That's a record. I did it for you.`,`[shy] Sunset tonight? I'll save you the edge of the pier.`,`[laugh] I wrote another poem. It rhymes 'farmer' with 'charmer'. I'm not proud.`],married:[`[happy] Morning! I went out early and the fish were biting. Well, early for me. Nine-ish.`,`[laugh] I sang to the hens this morning. I think they liked it. One of them laid an egg in protest.`,`[shy] I don't watch the sea for boats any more. I watch the road for you.`,`[happy] Sunset on the porch tonight? The farm has a pretty good one too, it turns out.`,`Mum keeps sending pies up the road. We'll never need to cook again. I'm not complaining.`],gifts:[{item:`sardine`,line:`[happy] Caught you a sardine before work. Fresh as anything. Don't let the cat see.`},{item:`mackerel`,line:`[laugh] Mackerel! A big one. I named it, then I remembered I was bringing it to you. Sorry, Gerald.`}]},hazel:{id:`hazel`,hearts:[{title:`Race You`,summary:`Hazel raced you down the road. Whoever won, she says she let you.`,cutscene:[{say:`hazel`,text:`[laugh] Hey! Race you to the end of the road. Ready? GO! ...I said go! Why aren't you running?!`},{choice:[{label:`Run as hard as you can.`,then:[{say:`narrator`,text:`You ran. Hazel ran faster, laughing the whole way, and beat you by three lengths.`},{say:`hazel`,text:`[laugh] HA! Not bad, farmer! You'll make a decent racer yet. Same time tomorrow?`},{do:{friendship:`hazel`,points:50}}]},{label:`Let her win.`,then:[{say:`hazel`,text:`[angry] Did you just LET me win? Don't you dare. I don't want a win I didn't earn.`},{say:`hazel`,text:`[laugh] ...Rematch. Now. No mercy.`},{do:{friendship:`hazel`,points:20}}]}]}]},{title:`The Blue Ribbon`,summary:`Hazel told you about the prize ribbon on her dungarees: she won it at eleven, at the last Spring Fair.`,hints:[{from:`edda`,text:`[laugh] My granddaughter's been polishing that ribbon of hers again. Ask her about it. Mind you've got an hour spare.`}],cutscene:[{say:`hazel`,text:`[happy] You keep looking at my ribbon. It's okay. Everybody does. It's very blue.`},{say:`hazel`,text:`Best Young Handler, last Spring Fair, fifteen years ago. I was eleven. My calf was called Buttons and she was a menace.`},{say:`hazel`,text:`[sad] Nobody's won a ribbon since. That's why I want the Fair back. Some kid out there deserves a Buttons.`},{choice:[{label:`We'll make it happen.`,then:[{say:`hazel`,text:`[laugh] WE will? Yeah. Yeah, we will!`},{do:{friendship:`hazel`,points:50}}]},{label:`Tell me more about Buttons.`,then:[{say:`hazel`,text:`[laugh] She ate the judge's hat. Still won. That's a champion.`},{do:{friendship:`hazel`,points:40}}]}]}]},{title:`Little Penrose`,summary:`Hazel told you her parents took the ferry to the mainland when she was twelve. She stayed with Edda, and the animals.`,cutscene:[{say:`hazel`,text:`[angry] Someone called me 'little Penrose' again. I'm twenty-six! I run a whole ranch!`},{say:`hazel`,text:`[sad] ...Sorry. It's not the name. It's that it makes me feel twelve. That's when Mum and Dad took the ferry.`},{say:`hazel`,text:`They said the island was finished. I said it wasn't. They went, and I stayed with Gran and the cows.`},{choice:[{label:`You were right to stay.`,then:[{say:`hazel`,text:`[shy] You think so? ...Yeah. Yeah, I was. Thanks. I needed someone else to say it.`},{do:{friendship:`hazel`,points:60}}]},{label:`That must have hurt.`,then:[{say:`hazel`,text:`[sad] It did. Still does, a bit. But I'm not a quitter. Penroses aren't.`},{do:{friendship:`hazel`,points:40}}]}]}]},{title:`Before Dawn`,summary:`Hazel caught you up early and blurted out that she likes you. Then told you to go feed your animals.`,lead:`Hazel is up before anyone. Catch her early, before 9 am (8 hearts).`,when:{hour:[6,9]},cutscene:[{say:`hazel`,text:`[surprised] You're up! Nobody's up this early except me and the hens. And now you.`},{say:`narrator`,text:`The sky was pale pink and the grass was soaked. Hazel had straw in her hair and wasn't aware of it.`},{say:`hazel`,text:`[shy] Okay. I've been practising this on Clover. She didn't say anything, which I took as support.`},{say:`hazel`,text:`[shy] I like you. Like, LIKE you. You're not a quitter and you work hard and you laugh at my jokes, even the cow ones.`},{choice:[{label:`I like you too.`,then:[{say:`hazel`,text:`[laugh] YES! I mean. Cool. That's cool. ...YES!`},{do:{friendship:`hazel`,points:60}}]},{label:`Pick the straw out of her hair.`,then:[{say:`hazel`,text:`[shy] ...Was that there the whole time? Ugh. Don't answer. Don't stop either.`},{do:{friendship:`hazel`,points:60}}]}]},{say:`hazel`,text:`[angry] Okay! Good talk! Go feed your animals! Bye!`}]},{title:`Clover's Bell`,summary:`Hazel gave you Clover's old brass cowbell, polished up, so she'd always hear you coming.`,lead:`You're courting Hazel. Keep seeing her (10 hearts).`,cutscene:[{say:`hazel`,text:`[happy] Here. Take it. Careful, it's loud.`},{say:`narrator`,text:`A brass cowbell on a red leather strap, polished so bright you could see your face in it.`},{say:`hazel`,text:`Clover's first bell. She's had a bigger one for years, but I kept this. Now it's yours. So I'll always hear you coming.`},{say:`hazel`,text:`[shy] That's romantic. In ranch terms. Don't laugh.`},{choice:[{label:`Ring it.`,then:[{say:`hazel`,text:`[laugh] Every cow in the meadow just looked at you. Perfect.`}]},{label:`Kiss her.`,then:[{say:`hazel`,text:`[surprised] ...Okay. Okay! That's... yep. Good. Do that more.`}]}]},{do:{flag:`key:bell-hazel`}}]}],bouquet:[{say:`hazel`,text:`[surprised] Is that a bouquet? For me? Not for Gran? Not for a cow?`},{say:`hazel`,text:`[laugh] ...I'm not going to eat it, if that's what you're worried about. Probably.`},{say:`hazel`,text:`[shy] Yes! Obviously yes! I was going to ask YOU if you took any longer.`}],proposal:[{say:`hazel`,text:`[surprised] A heron pendant. You're... is this... you're asking me to MARRY you?`},{say:`hazel`,text:`[laugh] YES! YES YES YES! Gran! GRAN! ...She can't hear me from here. I'll tell her. I'll tell EVERYONE.`}],vows:[{say:`hazel`,text:`[happy] I don't quit. On animals, on this island, on anything. So I'm never quitting on you.`},{say:`hazel`,text:`I will! ...Was I meant to wait? I will.`}],afterVows:[{say:`hazel`,text:`[laugh] Gran says if you ever make me cry she'll knit you something itchy.`},{say:`hazel`,text:`[happy] Race you home, husband!`}],family:[`edda`],baby:[[{say:`hazel`,text:`[surprised] A baby? A tiny human? I've delivered about a hundred calves. How different can it be?`},{say:`hazel`,text:`[laugh] ...Gran says very. Okay. Yes. Let's. I'm so ready. I'm terrified. Both!`}],[{say:`hazel`,text:`[laugh] Another one? {child} needs someone to race.`},{say:`hazel`,text:`[happy] Yes. Let's. Penroses come in herds.`}]],newborn:[{say:`hazel`,text:`[laugh] Up before dawn and yelling about it. Oh, that's my kid all right.`}],courting:[`[laugh] Race you to the well later? Winner picks supper. I always win, so it's carrots.`,`[shy] Clover asked about you. She didn't, she's a cow. But she would.`,`[happy] I told Gran we're courting. She said 'about time' and went back to her loom.`],married:[`[happy] Morning! I did your animals already. And mine. And the neighbour's goat, by accident.`,`[laugh] I've been up since four! You're very cute asleep. You snore like a calf.`,`[shy] Best thing about this farm? Coming home to it. To you. Okay, that was soppy. Moving on.`,`[happy] Gran's knitting you a scarf. In summer. She says she's 'getting ahead'.`,`[angry] It's going to rain on wash day. I can feel it. I'm bringing the washing in early.`],gifts:[{item:`milk`,line:`[happy] Fresh milk from the ranch. Clover says hello.`},{item:`egg`,line:`[laugh] The hens laid extra today. I told them it was for you. They tried harder.`}]},wren:{id:`wren`,hearts:[{title:`One Summer`,summary:`You found Wren's spectacles for her (they were on her head). She came to the island for one summer, three summers ago.`,cutscene:[{say:`wren`,text:`[surprised] Oh! Have you seen my spectacles? Round, gold, about this big? I've looked everywhere.`},{choice:[{label:`Point at her head.`,then:[{say:`wren`,text:`[laugh] ...Oh, for goodness' sake. Thank you. That's the third time this week.`},{do:{friendship:`wren`,points:40}}]},{label:`Help her look under the desk first.`,then:[{say:`narrator`,text:`You both searched the schoolhouse for ten minutes before Pip, passing the window, yelled "THEY'RE ON YOUR HEAD".`},{say:`wren`,text:`[laugh] Well. That was a lovely ten minutes anyway.`},{do:{friendship:`wren`,points:40}}]}]},{say:`wren`,text:`I came here to study the glyphs for one summer. I packed for one summer. I still only own one coat.`},{say:`wren`,text:`[shy] That was three summers ago. I keep meaning to buy another coat. I keep finding reasons to stay instead.`}]},{title:`Tea and Glyphs`,summary:`Wren made you tea and taught you a glyph. It means "home". Or possibly "soup".`,cutscene:[{say:`wren`,text:`[happy] Perfect timing, the kettle's just boiled. Sit, sit. Mind the books. And those books. And that pile.`},{say:`wren`,text:`Here. Let me show you one. This curl, with the line under it. I think it means "home".`},{say:`wren`,text:`[laugh] Or possibly "soup". The two are written very similarly. The old keepers must have liked soup.`},{choice:[{label:`Home and soup are close enough.`,then:[{say:`wren`,text:`[laugh] You know, that's the wisest thing anyone's said about this archive in three years.`},{do:{friendship:`wren`,points:50}}]},{label:`Try to copy the glyph.`,then:[{say:`narrator`,text:`Your glyph came out looking like a startled duck.`},{say:`wren`,text:`[happy] Oh, that's not bad at all! That might be "duck". I'll check.`},{do:{friendship:`wren`,points:40}}]}]}]},{title:`Quietly Brave`,summary:`Wren told you her family thought studying old scripts was foolish. She came anyway, scared the whole way.`,cutscene:[{say:`wren`,text:`[sad] I had a letter from my mother today. She asks when I'm coming home to do something sensible.`},{say:`wren`,text:`My family thought old scripts were a waste of a good mind. I came here anyway. I was frightened the whole boat ride.`},{say:`wren`,text:`[sad] I'm frightened of most things, honestly. Storms. Deep water. Pip with a stick.`},{choice:[{label:`Being scared and going anyway is brave.`,then:[{say:`wren`,text:`[shy] ...Is it? I never thought of it that way. Thank you. I'll remember that.`},{do:{friendship:`wren`,points:60}}]},{label:`Pip with a stick is terrifying.`,then:[{say:`wren`,text:`[laugh] Isn't he? He calls it his "sword". I call it a hazard.`},{do:{friendship:`wren`,points:30}}]}]},{say:`wren`,text:`[happy] You make it easier, you know. Being brave. I'm not quite sure why.`}]},{title:`The Lighthouse Plan`,summary:`Wren showed you her sketch of the old north-cliff lighthouse and asked you to climb it with her one day. A date-plan.`,cutscene:[{say:`wren`,text:`[shy] I drew something. Don't look at the perspective, perspective is not my strength.`},{say:`narrator`,text:`A careful pencil sketch of a lighthouse on a cliff, with two tiny figures at the top, one holding a book.`},{say:`wren`,text:`The old lighthouse on the north cliff. I've always wanted to see it. I'd like to see it with you. When the mist allows.`},{say:`wren`,text:`[shy] It's a plan. A date. A date-plan. I've been rehearsing the word 'date' all week and I still said 'plan' first.`},{choice:[{label:`It's a date.`,then:[{say:`wren`,text:`[laugh] ...Oh good. Oh, good. I may need to sit down. I am sitting down. Good.`},{do:{friendship:`wren`,points:60}}]},{label:`Which one of those is me?`,then:[{say:`wren`,text:`[shy] The one without the book. Obviously. ...The one I'm looking at.`},{do:{friendship:`wren`,points:60}}]}]}]},{title:`Margins`,summary:`Wren gave you a little notebook of every word she has translated, with notes to you in the margins.`,lead:`You're courting Wren. Keep seeing her (10 hearts).`,cutscene:[{say:`wren`,text:`[shy] I've made you something. It's a book. Of course it's a book.`},{say:`narrator`,text:`A slim notebook in lavender cloth. Every glyph she has translated, one to a page, and in the margins, in tiny handwriting, notes to you.`},{say:`wren`,text:`"Home (or soup)." "Brave (see: you)." I'm sorry, I couldn't stop. The margins kept filling up.`},{say:`wren`,text:`[happy] Please don't return it. It's the only book I've ever wanted someone to keep.`},{choice:[{label:`I'll keep it always.`},{label:`Kiss her.`,then:[{say:`wren`,text:`[surprised] ...Oh. Oh my. I've lost my spectacles again. I don't mind at all.`}]}]},{do:{flag:`key:notebook-wren`}}]}],bouquet:[{say:`wren`,text:`[surprised] For me? Oh. Oh, they're lovely. I'm going to press one in a book. I'm going to press all of them.`},{say:`wren`,text:`[shy] Is this... are you asking... I'd very much like that. Yes. Yes, please.`}],proposal:[{say:`wren`,text:`[surprised] A heron pendant. I know what that means. I've read about it in four separate sources.`},{say:`wren`,text:`[happy] And I don't need a single one of them to tell me the answer. Yes. Oh, yes.`}],vows:[{say:`wren`,text:`[shy] I came for one summer and stayed for three. I'd like to stay for all the rest.`},{say:`wren`,text:`I'm frightened of most things. Not this. Not you. I will.`}],afterVows:[{say:`wren`,text:`[laugh] My mother will faint when she reads my letter. I'm going to enjoy writing it enormously.`},{say:`wren`,text:`[happy] I'm moving my books to Thistledown. All of them. I hope the floor holds.`}],family:[`kit`],baby:[[{say:`wren`,text:`[surprised] A baby? I've... actually, I've read a great deal about babies. Purely academically.`},{say:`wren`,text:`[shy] I'd like that more than I can say. And I can say quite a lot, usually. Yes.`}],[{say:`wren`,text:`[happy] Another? {child} has already chewed two of my books. A sibling to share the blame seems fair.`},{say:`wren`,text:`[laugh] Yes. Let's.`}]],newborn:[{say:`wren`,text:`[shy] Hello, little one. I have so many books to read you. Every single one.`}],courting:[`[happy] I wrote your name in the margin of the shrine records. By accident. Twice.`,`[shy] Tea after lessons? I'll even remember where I put the cups.`,`[laugh] Pip asked if we're courting. I said 'define courting'. He said 'gross'. I think that's a yes.`],married:[`[happy] Morning, love. I made toast. It's only a little burnt. I'm improving.`,`[laugh] I've found my spectacles in the bread bin. I have no memory of putting them there.`,`[shy] It's very quiet out here after the schoolhouse. I like it. I like the quiet with you in it.`,`[happy] I've started a little archive in the sitting room. Don't worry, it's only one bookcase. Two. Three.`,`My mother wrote back. She says she's coming to visit. I'm hiding the good teacups.`],gifts:[{item:`amethyst`,line:`[happy] For you. It was in the archive's mineral drawer, with a label saying "spare". I chose to believe it.`},{item:`quartz`,line:`Quartz. I found it on my walk home. It caught the light, and I thought of you.`}]},ivy:{id:`ivy`,hearts:[{title:`Don't Touch That`,summary:`You nearly touched one of Ivy's tools. Instead of yelling, she handed you a wrench and made you her assistant.`,cutscene:[{say:`ivy`,text:`[surprised] DON'T. Touch. That. That's my calibrated spanner. Nobody touches the calibrated spanner.`},{say:`ivy`,text:`[laugh] ...Okay, that was loud. Sorry. Here. You can hold this one. It's just a normal wrench. It's not even my favourite.`},{choice:[{label:`Hold it very, very still.`,then:[{say:`narrator`,text:`Something deep inside the machine went clunk, then whirr, then ding.`},{say:`ivy`,text:`[laugh] YES! You held it perfectly! You're hired. You're my assistant. There's no pay.`},{do:{friendship:`ivy`,points:50}}]},{label:`What does it do?`,then:[{say:`ivy`,text:`[happy] It holds the bit that holds the bit that makes the bit go round. Obviously.`},{do:{friendship:`ivy`,points:30}}]}]}]},{title:`Same Boat`,summary:`Ivy remembered the boat ride you shared, the morning the mist parted. She says she wasn't scared. She was taking notes.`,cutscene:[{say:`ivy`,text:`[happy] Hey. Do you remember the boat? The morning we came in?`},{say:`ivy`,text:`The captain cut the engine, everyone panicked, and then your pendant started glowing and the mist just... opened. Like a curtain.`},{say:`ivy`,text:`[laugh] Everyone else was praying. I was taking notes. Three pages. I drew your pendant from four angles.`},{choice:[{label:`I noticed you staring.`,then:[{say:`ivy`,text:`[shy] At the pendant! I was staring at the PENDANT. ...Mostly.`},{do:{friendship:`ivy`,points:50}}]},{label:`Were you scared?`,then:[{say:`ivy`,text:`[shy] A bit. Don't tell anyone. I'm meant to be fearless. It's my whole brand.`},{do:{friendship:`ivy`,points:50}}]}]}]},{title:`Controlled Explosion`,summary:`After a bang that was (mostly) on purpose, Ivy admitted she's never had anyone to show her inventions to.`,hints:[{from:`bram`,text:`[surprised] Was that a bang from the old mill just now? Do look in on Ivy, would you. Make sure she still has her eyebrows.`}],cutscene:[{say:`narrator`,text:`BANG. A puff of black smoke rolled out of the Works. Ivy came out after it, coughing, grinning, eyebrows mostly intact.`},{say:`ivy`,text:`[laugh] Totally on purpose! Controlled! Seventy percent controlled!`},{say:`ivy`,text:`[sad] ...On the mainland they called me a menace. Nobody wanted to see what I made. They just wanted me to stop making noise.`},{say:`ivy`,text:`You're the first person who comes running toward the bang instead of away from it.`},{choice:[{label:`Show me what you were making.`,then:[{say:`ivy`,text:`[happy] Really? REALLY? Okay. Okay okay. Goggles on. Stand there. No, there.`},{do:{friendship:`ivy`,points:60}}]},{label:`Are you hurt?`,then:[{say:`ivy`,text:`[shy] ...No. But thanks for asking. Nobody ever asks. They just ask if the building's okay.`},{do:{friendship:`ivy`,points:50}}]}]}]},{title:`The Clockwork Heron`,summary:`Ivy built you a tiny clockwork heron that flaps its wings. She told you not to read into it. Then told you to read into it.`,cutscene:[{say:`ivy`,text:`[shy] Okay. I made a thing. A small thing. It's not for anything. Wind it up. Gently! Gently.`},{say:`narrator`,text:`A brass heron no bigger than a teacup. When you turned the key, it lifted its wings, tilted its head, and gave one tiny tick of a bow.`},{say:`ivy`,text:`I built it for you. Don't read into it.`},{say:`ivy`,text:`[shy] ...Read into it. Please read into it. I'm bad at this part. Machines are easier.`},{choice:[{label:`I read into it.`,then:[{say:`ivy`,text:`[laugh] Oh thank goodness. I had a whole backup plan with fireworks.`},{do:{friendship:`ivy`,points:60}}]},{label:`It's wonderful. So are you.`,then:[{say:`ivy`,text:`[surprised] ...I need to sit down. On something not sharp. Give me a second.`},{do:{friendship:`ivy`,points:60}}]}]}]},{title:`Matching Goggles`,summary:`Ivy gave you a pair of brass goggles to match hers, so you can stand next to her when things go bang.`,lead:`You're courting Ivy. Keep seeing her (10 hearts).`,cutscene:[{say:`ivy`,text:`[happy] Put these on. Go on. Adjust the strap. There.`},{say:`narrator`,text:`Brass goggles, just like hers, polished until they shone, with your initials scratched into the rim.`},{say:`ivy`,text:`Now you can stand next to me when things go bang. Right next to me. That's where I want you.`},{say:`ivy`,text:`[shy] I've never made anything that was just... for someone. It's scarier than explosions.`},{choice:[{label:`We match now.`},{label:`Kiss her.`,then:[{say:`ivy`,text:`[surprised] ...The goggles clinked. Ha. Do it again. Goggles off this time.`}]}]},{do:{flag:`key:goggles-ivy`}}]}],bouquet:[{say:`ivy`,text:`[surprised] Flowers! For me? I don't even have a vase. I'll make one. Out of a pipe. It'll be great.`},{say:`ivy`,text:`[laugh] Yes! Courting! Me! With you! This is the best experiment I've ever been part of.`}],proposal:[{say:`ivy`,text:`[surprised] Is that a heron pendant? Are you... you're... hold on, my brain's overheating.`},{say:`ivy`,text:`[laugh] YES! Obviously yes! I've been running the numbers for months and every single one comes out you!`}],vows:[{say:`ivy`,text:`[happy] I break things. It's sort of my job. But I've never wanted to build anything as much as I want to build a life with you.`},{say:`ivy`,text:`I will. Controlled. One hundred percent.`}],afterVows:[{say:`ivy`,text:`[laugh] I rigged a little firework for after. Just a small one. Okay, a medium one.`},{say:`ivy`,text:`[shy] We came in on the same boat. Now we're going home to the same house. That's... yeah. That's good engineering.`}],family:[],baby:[[{say:`ivy`,text:`[surprised] A baby? A small person? With your patience and my... everything else?`},{say:`ivy`,text:`[happy] Yes. I'm already designing a cradle that rocks itself. It won't explode. Probably. Yes!`}],[{say:`ivy`,text:`[laugh] Another one? {child} needs a lab partner.`},{say:`ivy`,text:`[happy] Let's do it. I'll build a second self-rocking cradle. The first one only caught fire once.`}]],newborn:[{say:`ivy`,text:`[laugh] Look at those little hands. Already reaching for my tools. That's my kid.`}],courting:[`[laugh] I named a gear after you. It's the most reliable one. Don't let it go to your head.`,`[happy] Strong tea and you. Best two things on the island. In that order. No, the other order.`,`[shy] Come by the Works after dark? I want to show you something that glows.`],married:[`[happy] Morning! I fixed the kettle. It's faster now. Possibly too fast. Stand back when it whistles.`,`[laugh] I built a little gadget that waters the window boxes. It also waters the cat.`,`[shy] I used to lie awake thinking about machines. Now I lie awake thinking about how lucky I am. Then machines.`,`[happy] Strong tea's on. I made yours how you like it. Which is wrong, but I respect it.`,`Don't go in the shed. Surprise in progress. Nothing's on fire. Currently.`],gifts:[{item:`copper-ore`,line:`[happy] Spare copper! I had too much. That's a lie, there's no such thing. Take it anyway.`},{item:`iron-ore`,line:`[laugh] Iron ore from the scrap pile. Totally unexploded. Probably.`}]}},Bz=Object.values(zz).flatMap(e=>Iz(e)),Vz=`Pip's Treasure`,Hz=[{id:`pip-treasure-ask`,kind:`side`,story:Vz,title:`Shiny Stones`,requires:{done:`prologue-arrival`},when:{met:`pip`},trigger:{talk:`pip`},lead:`Pip Hollis is up to something. Talk to him in the village.`,summary:`Pip asked you for three shiny stones for his treasure che